<section id="how" class="py-5 border-top">
    <p class="zw-eyebrow mb-1">How it works</p>
    <h2 class="mb-2">Four steps, one webhook.</h2>
    <p class="zw-muted mb-4" style="max-width:56ch;">
        No new platform to learn — you're adding one step to a Zap you already built.
    </p>
    <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-4 g-3">
        <div class="col">
            <div class="zw-flow-step h-100">
                <span class="zw-flow-num">01</span>
                <h3>Add the automation</h3>
                <p>Name it, set how often it should run, and how much slack to give it before you'd call it overdue.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
            <div class="zw-flow-step h-100">
                <span class="zw-flow-num">02</span>
                <h3>Copy the ping URL</h3>
                <p class="mb-2">A unique URL is generated the moment you add the automation.</p>
                <span class="zw-ping-url" style="font-size:0.7rem;">
                    <code>https://zap-watch.runasp.net/ping/8f3a&hellip;</code>
                    <button type="button" class="zw-copy-btn" disabled>Copy</button>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
            <div class="zw-flow-step h-100">
                <span class="zw-flow-num">03</span>
                <h3>Add one step to the Zap</h3>
                <p>"Webhooks by Zapier" &rarr; POST to that URL. Last step, after everything else already runs.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
            <div class="zw-flow-step h-100">
                <span class="zw-flow-num">04</span>
                <h3>Get alerted, not surprised</h3>
                <p>Email + SMS the moment it goes quiet. Clears itself the next time it fires.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
